# flux materials (0.9.0)
item.fluxecho.flux_grit.name=Flux Grit
fluxecho.flux_grit.tip=§3The nexus's ash, sunk to the sea floor among this shore's shards§r\nOnly the Flux Shard Collector gives it off\nGrows into flux crystal in GT's autoclave with ender pearl dust and distilled water
item.fluxecho.flux_crystal.name=Flux Crystal
fluxecho.flux_crystal.tip=§3The ship's ash, grown back into bone§r\nThe Flux Nexus's frame, conduits and core are made of it
item.fluxecho.echo_crystal.name=Echo Crystal
fluxecho.echo_crystal.holds=§dHolds: %s · %s
fluxecho.echo_crystal.tip=§3One thing this world remembers for you§r\nThe entry itself is kept; the same entry can be pressed once a day\nResearch, modules and the Echo Archive take it
item.fluxecho.phase_alloy.name=Phase Alloy
fluxecho.phase_alloy.tip=§3Hull plate: the sea's phase lines drift slowly over it§r\nMade in GT's electric blast furnace (EV, 2700 K)\nPhase II of the nexus and the modules of the phase take it; GT's wiremill draws it into the wire of memory filament
item.fluxecho.resonant_glass.name=Resonant Glass
fluxecho.resonant_glass.tip=§3A porthole: its edge ripples when something turns outside§r\nManifested at the Flux Nexus once Phase II is researched\nThe Echo Dome Generator and the Tidal Well take it, the resonant windows later
item.fluxecho.phase_alloy_wire.name=Phase Alloy Wire
fluxecho.phase_alloy_wire.tip=§3A nerve that has not learned to remember yet§r\nDrawn in GT's wiremill (IV), eight to an ingot\nCoated with an echo crystal at the Flux Nexus it becomes memory filament
item.fluxecho.memory_filament.name=Memory Filament
fluxecho.memory_filament.tip=§3A nerve: it remembers what flows through it§r\nManifested at the Flux Nexus from the wiremill's phase alloy wire once Phase II is researched\nPhase III of the nexus, the outer ring and the phase's buildings take it
item.fluxecho.manifest_matter.name=Manifest Matter
fluxecho.manifest_matter.tip=§3This world's matter, learning the ship's shape for the first time§r\nManifested at a Flux Nexus of phase III or later from phase alloy, an echo crystal and an LuV circuit once the Sophon Array is researched; the table draws a great deal of power while it makes it\nPhase IV of the nexus, the sky ring, the anti-gravity lattice and the phase's buildings take it
item.fluxecho.anti_gravity_lattice.name=Anti-gravity Lattice
fluxecho.anti_gravity_lattice.tip=§3This world's matter, learning to float for the first time§r\nManifested at the Flux Nexus from manifest matter and resonant glass once the Mast is researched\nThe floating foundations of the sky ring's platforms and the sky ring's buildings take it

# flux frame (0.9.0)
tile.fluxecho.frame.base.name=Flux Frame Base
fluxecho.frame.base.tip=§3The floor of the Flux Nexus§r\nMost of its octagonal base
tile.fluxecho.frame.base_lit.name=Lit Frame Base
fluxecho.frame.base_lit.tip=§3A base with a conduit line in it§r\nThe eight spokes of the Flux Nexus's base that carry the flux to the middle
tile.fluxecho.frame.pillar.name=Frame Pillar
fluxecho.frame.pillar.tip=§3The frame's bones§r\nIn a Flux Nexus they turn into curved ribs you can walk through once it forms; an Echo Archive's corners and eaves are made of them too
tile.fluxecho.frame.conduit.name=Flux Conduit
fluxecho.frame.conduit.tip=§3A pillar with the flux running inside§r\nThe column in the middle of the Flux Nexus; once formed it turns into a column of light
tile.fluxecho.frame.ring.name=Ring Segment
fluxecho.frame.ring.tip=§3A piece of a ring§r\nThe sixteen on top of the Flux Nexus float up and turn once it forms
tile.fluxecho.frame.seat.name=Crystal Seat
fluxecho.frame.seat.tip=§3Where the core sits§r\nThe heart of the Flux Nexus; once formed the core floats in the air
tile.fluxecho.frame.foundation.name=Module Foundation
fluxecho.frame.foundation.tip=§3The ground a module stands on§r\nThe Echo Archive and the other modules are built on it
tile.fluxecho.frame.shelf.name=Echo Shelf
fluxecho.frame.shelf.tip=§3A shelf for one book§r\nThe walls of the Echo Archive. Once it forms, walk in: right-click with a sample to shelve it, with an empty hand to take it down, with a blank index card to write one
tile.fluxecho.frame.console.name=Console Stand
fluxecho.frame.console.tip=§3A waist-high stand§r\nUnder the Flux Nexus's core it puts the core at eye height; the reading desk in the middle of a library's hall is one too\nOnce formed, right-click it to open its machine's GUI
tile.fluxecho.frame.anchor.name=Cladding Anchor
fluxecho.frame.anchor.tip=§3A frame block with a hexagonal socket plate on each face§r\nThe city's buildings carry a few of them; the claddings of later versions will grow from them
tile.fluxecho.frame.float.name=Floating Foundation
fluxecho.frame.float.tip=§3An anti-gravity lattice cube: a grid to walk on, a lifting glow under it§r\nThe decks of the sky ring's platforms, floating over the city
tile.fluxecho.deck.deck.name=Campus Deck
fluxecho.deck.deck.tip=§3The campus floor: all the ground around the nexus is paved with it§r
tile.fluxecho.deck.trim.name=Trim Steel
