fluxecho.fitting.tread.tip=§3A half-high step for stairs§r
tile.fluxecho.fitting.glaze.name=Steel Glaze
fluxecho.fitting.glaze.tip=§3Steel-framed glass: a module's windows§r
tile.fluxecho.fitting.pedestal.name=Holo Pedestal
fluxecho.fitting.pedestal.tip=§3A low stand for a hologram§r
tile.fluxecho.fitting.socket.name=Sample Socket
fluxecho.fitting.socket.tip=§3A column with a lit recess in each side§r\nA unit of a city module keeps one sample in it, floating in the recess
tile.fluxecho.fitting.basin.name=Basin Rim
fluxecho.fitting.basin.tip=§3A low rim with a lit lip§r\nThe edge of a planter bed or a pond; rims side by side join up
tile.fluxecho.fitting.lift.name=Light Lift Pad
fluxecho.fitting.lift.tip=§3A flush plate with an iris of light§r\nPads stacked in one column make a light lift: stand on one and jump to rise to the next pad up, sneak to sink to the next pad down\nOn the way you pass through the pads and the nexus's own blocks in the shaft, and take no fall damage

# flux nexus, research, library (0.9.0)
tile.fluxecho.nexus.name=Flux Nexus
fluxecho.nexus.tip=§3The nexus pinned into the flux layer: research, manifestation and modules start here§r\nDraws its upkeep from the team wireless network\nFormed: curved ribs hold a turning ring, the core floats in its middle, a beam runs up into the sky
fluxecho.nexus.place_hint=§7Right-click the ground: the core goes two blocks up, and the nexus surveys, projects and, once you press Start, builds itself§r\n§7Place it sneaking: just the core, built by hand the 0.9.2 way§r
fluxecho.nexus.carries_credit=§bCarries build credit§r: %s materials, %s parts, %s kinds from the recycle store
fluxecho.nexus.carries_pending=§bCarries an unfinished manifestation§r: %s × %s
fluxecho.nexus.carries_campus=§bCarries its campus§r: put it back where it stood (%s) and the campus carries on
fluxecho.nexus.carries_overflow=§bAnother %s kinds from the recycle store§r are kept for your team: they come back into the recycle store of your team's nexus as it has room
fluxecho.nexus.structure=§bPhase I: an 11×11 octagonal base, 6 high§r\n· Base: Flux Frame Base, the eight spokes Lit Frame Base\n· Middle: three Flux Conduits, a Crystal Seat on top\n· The four diagonals: Frame Pillars, 2 high three blocks out, then 2 high one block further in (curved ribs once formed)\n· Layer 6: a ring of 16 Ring Segments\n· The core sits on the front rim of the base, two blocks above it (a Console Stand under it), facing out\n· Each later phase adds a stage on top: pillars, conduits, a seat, a ring; from phase II the middle of the base is a Light Lift Pad (the nexus grows itself once the phase is researched)\nStructureLib's hologram projector previews and builds it\nNEI preview: tiers 1–5 are phases I–V, 6–10 the same with the city standing round it, each building of the phase on its site
