fluxecho.library.tip=§3The Flux Nexus's first module, the codex made real§r\nA library to walk into: every shelf holds one sample as a book\nThe whole team's echo machines borrow from it; it works while docked on a slot of a nexus's inner ring
fluxecho.library.structure=§bThe Echo Archive: a two-storey library 27×35 and 16 high§r\n· The nexus's construction raises it on a hall site: once the library is researched the nexus projects it, and with the materials supplied it builds itself block by block\n· 78 bookcases of 9 books each, 702 in all; a bookcase is used as a whole: right-click any part of it\n· The core between the two front doors, two blocks above the foundation, facing the nexus\n· Made of Module Foundation, Echo Shelves and Console Stands; Campus Deck, Lit Deck, Wall Panels, Lit Wall Panels, Dark Wainscot and Light Cornice; and the fittings Shelf Post, Shelf Plinth, Shelf Crown, Gallery Rail, Stair Tread, Steel Glaze and Holo Pedestal (NEI shows it in 3D with its materials)\n§3The 0.9.2 library hall still forms§r: 11×11 and 8 high on a 13×13 module foundation, walls of Echo Shelves 5 high, 167 books\nStructureLib's hologram projector previews and builds it
fluxecho.module.eco_dome=Eco Dome
tile.fluxecho.module_core.eco_dome.name=Eco Dome Core
fluxecho.eco_dome.tip=§3The Flux Nexus's greenhouse§r\nA glass dome with floating garden islands round a tree of light\nTwelve planters keep the team's bee, sapling, seed and butterfly samples; it works while docked on its nexus and powered from the team wireless network
fluxecho.eco_dome.structure=§bThe Eco Dome: a glass dome 27×35 and 21 high§r\n· The nexus's construction raises it on a hall site (to the nexus's right first, then its left, then behind it): once the Eco Dome is researched the nexus projects it, and with the materials supplied it builds itself block by block\n· A portal block before a glazed drum and dome; inside, a gallery, two floating islands and a world tree of light\n· 12 planters of 3 Sample Sockets each, 36 samples; a planter is used as a whole: right-click any part of it holding a sample to plant it, empty-handed to open the dome; sneak-click a socket empty-handed to take its sample back\n· The core in the portal between the two doors, two blocks above the foundation, facing the nexus\n· Made of Module Foundation and frame parts, Campus Deck and Wall Panels, Steel Glaze, Basin Rims, Sample Sockets and Cladding Anchors (NEI shows it in 3D with its materials)\nStructureLib's hologram projector previews and builds it
fluxecho.unit.planter=Planter
fluxecho.module.dome_generator=Echo Dome Generator
tile.fluxecho.module_core.dome_generator.name=Echo Dome Generator Core
fluxecho.dome_generator.tip=§3The pod at the zenith that will raise the team's dome§r\nA saucer forty blocks over the nexus (lower over high ground) on six curved legs; the light lift on the nexus rises to it\nSeven ward consoles keep one function core each; it works while docked on its nexus and powered from the team wireless network
fluxecho.dome_generator.structure=§bThe Echo Dome Generator: a saucer pod 21×21 and 10 high, forty blocks over the nexus (lower over high ground), on six legs§r\n· The nexus's construction raises it at the zenith once the Echo Dome is researched (phase II): the six legs from the forum first, then the pod in the air; supply the core and materials and press Start\n· The pod: a glazed ring room round a light-lift pad, a saucer roof with six emitter nodes; the eight door openings and the shaft over the pad are glazed and capped until the sky ring and the orbit open them\n· 7 ward consoles of 1 Sample Socket each: right-click one holding a function core to set it, empty-handed to open the generator\n· The core four blocks in front of the pad, two above the pod floor, facing the gate\n· The legs and the emitter nodes give way to rendered ribs and arcs once it forms; from phase IV it floats without its legs\n· Made of Module Foundation and frame parts, Campus Deck and Wall Panels, Steel Glaze, Sample Sockets and a Light Lift Pad (NEI shows it in 3D with its materials)\nStructureLib's hologram projector previews and builds it
fluxecho.unit.ward=Ward Console
fluxecho.module.root=Tidal Well
fluxecho.module.root.deep=Deep Root
tile.fluxecho.module_core.root.name=Tidal Well Core
fluxecho.root.tip=§3The well under the nexus, where the flux layer's tide wells up§r\nA shaft up to 26 blocks deep under the forum; the light lift on the nexus sinks to the island in its tidal pool\nEight tide taps keep one fuel each; it works while docked on its nexus and powered from the team wireless network
fluxecho.root.structure=§bThe Tidal Well: an octagonal shaft 25×25, from just under the forum up to 26 blocks down§r\n· The nexus's construction sinks it under the dais once the Tidal Well is researched (phase II): layer by layer from the lid down, each layer's wall before its inside is dug; then it drains what water came in and lays the floor and the fittings. Supply the core and materials and press Start\n· The nexus's base must be at Y 14 or higher; under Y 32 the well is shallower (20, 14 or 8 blocks deep) and keeps its 8 taps\n· Inside: walls with three flux-layer bands, the tidal pool round an island with a light-lift pad, four bridges, a walkway, three tidal rings over the water and a helix ramp up the wall (a shallower well has fewer bands and rings)\n· 8 tide taps of 1 Sample Socket each in the pool's rim: right-click one holding a fuel to set it, empty-handed to open the well\n· From phase IV, with the Deep Root researched, the well grows into the Deep Root: a chamber 13 or 7 layers deep under the well where the ground has room (down to Y0-39), or over lower ground the roots come down into the well itself; 8 root bays of 1 Sample Socket each join the taps\n· The core on the island, two blocks in front of the pad on a Console Stand, at eye height, facing the gate\n· Once it forms the tidal rings give way to rendered rings that rise and fall with the tide\n· Made of Module Foundation and frame parts, Campus Deck and Wall Panels, Basin Rims, Sample Sockets, water and a Light Lift Pad (NEI shows it in 3D with its materials)\nStructureLib's hologram projector previews and builds it
fluxecho.unit.tap=Tide Tap
fluxecho.unit.bay=Root Bay
fluxecho.module.arcane_court=Arcane Court
tile.fluxecho.module_core.arcane_court.name=Arcane Court Core
fluxecho.arcane_court.tip=§3The Flux Nexus's arcane court§r\nAn octagonal hall under a steep hollow spire, three rings of ink turning round it\nIts infusion circle, cauldrons, aspect pillars and desks keep the team's thaumic samples; it works while docked on its nexus and powered from the team wireless network
fluxecho.arcane_court.structure=§bThe Arcane Court: an octagonal pavilion 25×25 and 33 high under a spire§r\n· The nexus's construction raises it on a diagonal pavilion site (site 7 first, then 1, 5, 3) once the Arcane Court is researched (phase II): the nexus projects it; supply the core and materials and press Start\n· Four chamfer portals lead along the diagonals to the altar at its heart; slit windows in the octagon's walls, a hollow spire over them whose finial gives way to a rendered violet crystal once it forms\n· 21 units, 44 samples: the infusion circle (8 Sample Sockets), 4 cauldrons, 8 aspect pillars (3 Sample Sockets each), 8 research desks; a unit is used as a whole: right-click any part of it holding a sample to set it, empty-handed to open the court; sneak-click a socket empty-handed to take its sample back\n· The core on the central altar's Console Stand, two blocks above the foundation\n· Made of Module Foundation and frame parts, Campus Deck and Wall Panels, Steel Glaze, Basin Rims, Sample Sockets, plinths and crowns, and Cladding Anchors (NEI shows it in 3D with its materials)\nStructureLib's hologram projector previews and builds it
fluxecho.unit.infusion=Infusion Circle
fluxecho.unit.cauldron=Cauldron
fluxecho.unit.pillar=Aspect Pillar
fluxecho.unit.desk=Research Desk
fluxecho.module.blood_covenant=Blood Covenant Altar
tile.fluxecho.module_core.blood_covenant.name=Blood Covenant Altar Core
fluxecho.blood_covenant.tip=§3The Flux Nexus's blood altar§r\nA red rotunda stepped in three tiers round an open oculus, the blood orb floating over it\nIts orb cradles and ritual stones keep the team's blood magic samples; it works while docked on its nexus and powered from the team wireless network
fluxecho.blood_covenant.structure=§bThe Blood Covenant Altar: an octagonal pavilion 25×25 and 17 high in three stepped tiers§r\n· The nexus's construction raises it on a diagonal pavilion site (site 5 first, then 3, 7, 1) once the Blood Covenant Altar is researched (phase II): the nexus projects it; supply the core and materials and press Start\n· Four chamfer portals lead to the dais at its heart; inside, a stepped funnel rises to the open oculus over the altar, and a railed terrace runs round the first tier\n· 12 units, 12 samples: 8 orb cradles and 4 ritual stones, each in the middle of an altar bay marked in the floor (5×5, room for your own blood altar); a unit is used as a whole: right-click any part of it holding a sample to set it, empty-handed to open the altar; sneak-click a socket empty-handed to take its sample back\n· The core over the altar's Console Stand on the dais, three blocks above the foundation\n· Made of Module Foundation and frame parts, Campus Deck and Wall Panels, Stair Treads, Gallery Rails, plinths, Sample Sockets and Cladding Anchors (NEI shows it in 3D with its materials)\nStructureLib's hologram projector previews and builds it
fluxecho.unit.cradle=Orb Cradle
fluxecho.unit.ritual=Ritual Stone
fluxecho.module.hunting_ground=Echo Hunting Ground
tile.fluxecho.module_core.hunting_ground.name=Echo Hunting Ground Core
fluxecho.hunting_ground.tip=§3The Flux Nexus's hunting ground§r\nAn open amphitheatre round a holo arena under an amber canopy of light\nIts imprint consoles keep the team's mob imprints; it works while docked on its nexus and powered from the team wireless network
fluxecho.hunting_ground.structure=§bThe Echo Hunting Ground: an octagonal amphitheatre 25×25 and 10 high§r\n· The nexus's construction raises it on a diagonal pavilion site (site 3 first, then 5, 1, 7) once the Echo Hunting Ground is researched (phase II): the nexus projects it; supply the core and materials and press Start\n· Four chamfer portals and the vomitoria under the seats lead to the arena at its heart, a holo grid round the emitter; half-block terraces rise round it to the wall, and the velarium's ring over the top terraces gives way to a rendered canopy once it forms\n· 12 imprint consoles of 1 Sample Socket each on the arena's rim, 12 samples: right-click one holding an imprint to set it, empty-handed to open the ground; sneak-click a socket empty-handed to take its sample back\n· The core on the emitter's Console Stand at the arena's centre, two blocks above the foundation\n· Made of Module Foundation and frame parts, Campus Deck, Grate Deck and Wall Panels, Steel Glaze, Stair Treads, plinths, Holo Pedestals, Sample Sockets and Cladding Anchors (NEI shows it in 3D with its materials)\nStructureLib's hologram projector previews and builds it
fluxecho.unit.imprint=Imprint Console
fluxecho.module.mana_fountain=Mana Fountain Array
tile.fluxecho.module_core.mana_fountain.name=Mana Fountain Array Core
fluxecho.mana_fountain.tip=§3The Flux Nexus's fountain court§r\nA cloister round a court of fountains and a magic circle, a spout of mana rising from its obelisk\nIts fountains and flower urns keep the team's Botania samples; it works while docked on its nexus and powered from the team wireless network
fluxecho.mana_fountain.structure=§bThe Mana Fountain Array: an octagonal cloister 25×25 and 8 high§r\n· The nexus's construction raises it on a diagonal pavilion site (site 1 first, then 7, 3, 5) once the Mana Fountain Array is researched (phase II): the nexus projects it; supply the core and materials and press Start\n· Four chamfer portals lead under a glass-roofed arcade and through a colonnade into an open court with a magic circle; the arcade's floor is grass for your own flowers and mana pools, and the obelisk's top gives way to a rendered spout of mana once it forms\n· 16 units, 16 samples: 8 fountains (a Sample Socket over the water in a ring of Basin Rims) and 8 flower urns; a unit is used as a whole: right-click any part of it holding a sample to set it, empty-handed to open the array; sneak-click a socket empty-handed to take its sample back\n· The core on the obelisk's Console Stand at the court's centre, two blocks above the foundation\n· Made of Module Foundation and frame parts, Campus Deck and Wall Panels, Steel Glaze, posts, plinths, Basin Rims, Sample Sockets, water and Cladding Anchors (NEI shows it in 3D with its materials)\nStructureLib's hologram projector previews and builds it
fluxecho.unit.fountain=Fountain
fluxecho.unit.urn=Flower Urn
fluxecho.module.resonance_gate=Resonance Gate
tile.fluxecho.module_core.resonance_gate.name=Resonance Gate Core
fluxecho.resonance_gate.tip=§3The Flux Nexus's gate§r\nTwo wing towers either side of the gate road joined by a bridge, a crystal spire floating and slowly turning over it\nIts resonators and tuning racks keep the team's samples; it works while docked on its nexus and powered from the team wireless network
fluxecho.resonance_gate.structure=§bThe Resonance Gate: a gatehouse 31×17 and 18 high§r\n· The nexus's construction raises it on the gate (site 0) once the Resonance Gate is researched (phase II): the nexus projects it; supply the core and materials and press Start\n· Two wing towers (9×17 each) stand either side of the gate road, the passage between them 13 wide and 7 high left open: the gate road, its widenings and the four pylons stay as they are, and only the ground the road leaves bare is floored\n· Each wing has a ground hall (a front door and a door onto the passage) and a spiral stair up to its upper hall 8 blocks up; both upper halls open into the resonance chamber on the bridge, whose core column gives way to a rendered crystal spire once it forms\n· 10 units, 24 samples: 6 resonator columns (2 samples each) in the resonance chamber and 4 tuning racks (3 samples each) on the halls' outer walls; a unit is used as a whole: right-click any part of it holding a sample to set it, empty-handed to open the gate; sneak-click a socket empty-handed to take its sample back\n· The core on the Console Stand of the kiosk in the road under the bridge, two blocks above the foundation, in reach from the road\n· Made of Module Foundation and frame parts, Campus Deck and Wall Panels, Steel Glaze, posts, plinths, crowns, treads, holo pedestals, Sample Sockets and Cladding Anchors (NEI shows it in 3D with its materials)\nStructureLib's hologram projector previews and builds it
fluxecho.unit.resonator=Resonator
fluxecho.unit.rack=Tuning Rack
fluxecho.module.dual_foil_vault=Dual-foil Vault
tile.fluxecho.module_core.dual_foil_vault.name=Dual-foil Vault Core
fluxecho.dual_foil_vault.tip=§3The Flux Nexus's vault§r\nA windowless monolith 27 high whose whole front is one giant canvas, a gallery of canvases inside\nIts canvases and the foil keep the team's items, one kind each; it works while docked on its nexus and powered from the team wireless network
fluxecho.dual_foil_vault.structure=§bThe Dual-foil Vault: a monolith 27×35 and 27 high§r\n· The nexus's construction raises it on a hall site (to the nexus's left first, then its right, then behind it) once the Dual-foil Vault is researched (phase II): the nexus projects it; supply the core and materials and press Start\n· A windowless hall under a sawtooth roof with six skylights; over its doors the whole front is one canvas 17×12 in a lit frame\n· Inside one nave open to the roof: both long walls carry three tiers of seven canvases; two corner tower stairs climb to catwalks 8 and 16 blocks up, and a cross walk passes over the foil on the back wall\n· 43 units, 43 items: 42 canvases (3 plinths, 3×4 Canvas Panels and 3 crowns each) and the foil (13×11 Canvas Panels over the desk); a unit is used as a whole: right-click any part of it holding an item to put it in, empty-handed to open the vault; sneak-click it empty-handed to take its item back\n· The core in the portal between the two doors, two blocks above the foundation, facing the nexus; the desk's Console Stand under the foil opens the vault too\n· Made of Module Foundation and frame parts, Campus Deck, Wall Panels and Canvas Panels, Steel Glaze, posts, plinths, crowns, rails, treads, holo pedestals and Cladding Anchors (NEI shows it in 3D with its materials)\nStructureLib's hologram projector previews and builds it
fluxecho.unit.canvas=Canvas
fluxecho.unit.foil=Foil
fluxecho.module.sophon_array=Sophon Array
tile.fluxecho.module_core.sophon_array.name=Sophon Array Core
fluxecho.sophon_array.tip=§3The Flux Nexus's sophon array§r\nA lattice sphere on a podium round a point of light, a data hall inside the podium\nIts memory racks keep the team's samples; it works while docked on its nexus and powered from the team wireless network
fluxecho.sophon_array.structure=§bThe Sophon Array: an octagonal podium 31×31 under a lattice sphere, 33 high§r\n· The nexus's construction raises it on an outer diagonal (O1 first, then O7, O3, O5) once the Sophon Array is researched (phase III) and the outer ring is laid: the nexus projects it; supply the core and materials and press Start\n· An octagonal podium 5 high with four chamfer portals and a glazed oculus in its roof; on the roof four struts hold a lattice sphere of radius 12 (a meridian every 30°, a parallel every 4 layers), and once it forms struts and lattice give way to a rendered spherical frame round a point of light\n· 48 units, 144 samples: two rows of memory racks on each side of the data hall (a plinth, 3 Sample Sockets and a crown each, floor to ceiling), the four diagonal paths from the portals left clear; a unit is used as a whole: right-click any part of it holding a sample to set it, empty-handed to open the array; sneak-click a socket empty-handed to take its sample back\n· The core on the Console Stand at the hall's centre under the oculus, two blocks above the foundation; look up through the glass to see the point of light\n· Made of Module Foundation and frame parts, Campus Deck and Wall Panels, Steel Glaze, plinths, crowns, Sample Sockets and Cladding Anchors (NEI shows it in 3D with its materials)\nStructureLib's hologram projector previews and builds it
fluxecho.unit.memory_rack=Memory Rack
fluxecho.module.holo_table=Holo Sand Table
tile.fluxecho.module_core.holo_table.name=Holo Sand Table Core
fluxecho.holo_table.tip=§3The Flux Nexus's holo sand table§r\nA rotunda under a shallow dome, a round table under a hanging ring of light where the whole base turns as a hologram\nIts table takes 9 samples and its nine layer consoles keep nothing (layers come in a later version); it works while docked on its nexus and powered from the team wireless network
fluxecho.holo_table.structure=§bThe Holo Sand Table: an octagonal rotunda 31×31 and 16 high§r\n· The nexus's construction raises it on an outer diagonal (O7 first, then O1, O5, O3) once the Holo Sand Table is researched (phase III) and the outer ring is laid: the nexus projects it; supply the core and materials and press Start\n· A drum 9 high with four chamfer portals and a glazed band under a shallow stepped dome and a glazed lantern; two mirrored ramps climb the drum's sides to a railed gallery 6 up at the back, looking down on the table\n· 10 units, 9 samples: the round table of radius 4.5 at the centre (plinths round a top of Steel Glaze, one unit of 9 samples) and nine layer consoles round it (they keep nothing; right-click one to open its own page in the module window); a ring of Ring Segments hangs over the table and gives way to a rendered ring of light once it forms; right-click any part of the table holding a sample to set it, empty-handed to open the table\n· The core on the Console Stand at the table's front, two blocks above the foundation\n· Made of Module Foundation and frame parts, Campus Deck and Wall Panels, Steel Glaze, plinths, rails, treads, Ring Segments and Cladding Anchors (NEI shows it in 3D with its materials)\nStructureLib's hologram projector previews and builds it
