fluxecho.module.sky_sails=Sky Sail Array
tile.fluxecho.module_core.sky_sails.name=Sky Sail Array Core
fluxecho.sky_sails.tip=§3The Flux Nexus's sky sails§r\nA bridge cabin on a floating platform and six masts, three huge sails of light spread between them, turned toward the sun\nEach mast keeps a sail; it works while docked on its nexus and powered from the team wireless network
fluxecho.sky_sails.structure=§bThe Sky Sail Array: a floating platform 21×21 and 15 high§r\n· The nexus's construction raises it on the sky ring (S2 first, then S6) once the Sky Sail Array is researched (phase IV) and the dome generator's pod floats: the nexus projects it; supply the core and materials and press Start. The job also lays the catwalk from the pod and opens the pod's door to it\n· A platform of Floating Foundation level with the pod's floor, railed round but for the catwalk's mouth; a bridge cabin at the front (walls 4 high, the kit portal, a back door, two holo pedestals inside) and six masts behind it in three pairs (a plinth, a Sample Socket, ten posts and a crown, 13 high), the light sails drawn between each pair\n· 6 units, 6 samples: each mast's plinth and socket; right-click either holding a sample to set it, empty-handed to open the array\n· The core in the cabin's portal between its two doors, two blocks above the deck, facing the pod\n· Made of Floating Foundation and frame parts, Wall Panels, Steel Glaze, posts, plinths, crowns, rails, holo pedestals and Sample Sockets (NEI shows it in 3D with its materials)\nStructureLib's hologram projector previews and builds it
fluxecho.unit.mast=Sail Mast
fluxecho.module.observatory=Observatory
tile.fluxecho.module_core.observatory.name=Observatory Core
fluxecho.observatory.tip=§3The Flux Nexus's observatory§r\nAn observing room under a stepped dome with a meridian slit on a floating platform over the Archive, a telescope inside and a ring lens floating over the dome\nIts seven lens cases keep the team's samples; it works while docked on its nexus and powered from the team wireless network
fluxecho.observatory.structure=§bThe Observatory: a floating platform 21×21 and 13 high§r\n· The nexus's construction raises it on the sky ring behind the nexus (S4) once the Observatory is researched (phase IV) and the dome generator's pod floats: the nexus projects it; supply the core and materials and press Start. The job also lays the catwalk from the pod and opens the pod's door to it\n· A platform of Floating Foundation level with the pod's floor, railed round but for the catwalk's mouth; a vestibule with the kit portal opens into an octagonal observing room (walls 5 high, a Light Cornice) under a hollow stepped dome with a glazed meridian slit; in the middle the telescope pier (a Console Stand, Frame Pillars and a Crystal Seat; the whole pier, console, pillars and seat, gives way to the rendered telescope once it forms)\n· 7 units, 7 samples: seven lens cases round the wall (a plinth and a Sample Socket each); right-click either holding a sample to set it, empty-handed to open the observatory\n· The core in the vestibule's portal between its two doors, two blocks above the deck, facing the pod\n· Made of Floating Foundation and frame parts, Wall Panels and Lit Wall Panels, Steel Glaze, posts, plinths, rails and Sample Sockets (NEI shows it in 3D with its materials)\nStructureLib's hologram projector previews and builds it
fluxecho.unit.lens=Lens Case
