tile.fluxecho.module_core.droplet_hangar.name=Droplet Hangar Core
fluxecho.droplet_hangar.tip=§3The Flux Nexus's droplet hangar§r\nEight cradles on a floating platform round a control kiosk, a mirror droplet hovering over each\nEach cradle keeps a droplet; it works while docked on its nexus and powered from the team wireless network
fluxecho.droplet_hangar.structure=§bThe Droplet Hangar: a floating platform 21×21 and 7 high§r\n· The nexus's construction raises it on the sky ring (S6 first, then S2) once the Droplet Hangar is researched (phase IV) and the dome generator's pod floats: the nexus projects it; supply the core and materials and press Start. The job also lays the catwalk from the pod and opens the pod's door to it\n· A platform of Floating Foundation level with the pod's floor, railed round but for the catwalk's mouth; the control kiosk at the front under a canopy of Ring Segments (they give way to a rendered ring of light once it forms)\n· 8 units, 8 samples: eight droplet cradles in four mirrored pairs (a 3×3 Basin Rim round a Sample Socket); right-click any part of one holding a sample to set it, empty-handed to open the hangar\n· The core on the kiosk's Console Stand, two blocks above the deck, facing the pod\n· Made of Floating Foundation and frame parts, rails, Basin Rims and Sample Sockets (NEI shows it in 3D with its materials)\nStructureLib's hologram projector previews and builds it
